---
import FieldGuideLayout from '../../../components/FieldGuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<FieldGuideLayout
  title="Content cache"
  description="Runtime asset loader. Master table at 0x020AA740, 712 references. Path strings live in a 28 KB region at 0x020A1000."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: 'How the Game Works', href: `${base}/field-guide/how-the-game-works/` },
    { label: 'Content cache' },
  ]}
>
  <h2>Master cache table</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Symbol</th><th>RAM</th><th>Refs in arm9</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>master cache table</td><td><code>0x020AA740</code></td><td>712</td><td>Indexed pointer-to-asset table; each slot identifies one loaded resource.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>path string region</td><td><code>0x020A1000..0x020A8000</code></td><td>—</td><td>~28 KB of static path strings (131 unique paths). Each path is a NUL-terminated ASCII string like <code>"item/itemicon.ofs"</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>game state struct (pointer)</td><td><code>0x021A55C0</code></td><td>750</td><td>Pointer to runtime game state; most engine functions take this in R0.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Generic loader</h2>
  <p>
    All asset load requests funnel through the generic loader
    <code>FUN_02009894</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`FUN_02009894(
    void *table,        // r0 — usually 0x020AA740
    const char *path,   // r1 — pointer into 0x020A1000..0x020A8000
    u16 sub_index,      // r2 — TOC entry index inside the container
    u32 size,           // r3 — expected payload size (or 0 = use TOC length)
    u32 flag1,          // stack
    u32 type_code,      // stack — e.g. 0x7800 for item icons
    u32 flag2,          // stack
    u32 flag3           // stack
);`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The loader reads the file at <code>path</code> from the NDS filesystem,
    decompresses it if LZS-wrapped, walks its RESO TOC to find
    <code>sub_index</code>, and writes a pointer/handle into the master
    cache table at the slot the caller has prepared.
  </p>

  <h2>Documented loader call sites</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Caller</th><th>Path</th><th>Asset class</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>ov003</td><td><code>2d/buyitem.lzs</code></td><td>Shop chrome</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ov003</td><td><code>2d/itemorderwnd.lzs</code></td><td>Shop order window</td></tr>
      <tr><td>arm9 <code>0x02052D20</code></td><td><code>item/itemicon.ofs</code></td><td>Item icon (per item-icon index)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>arm9 <code>0x02052D20</code></td><td><code>global.lzs</code> entry 5</td><td>Item icon palette (256-color)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>arm9 (boot)</td><td><code>global.lzs</code> entry 0</td><td>Font (NFTR)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ov137</td><td><code>2d/inputmagic/mgcall.ofs</code></td><td>Magic glyph atlas</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ov137</td><td><code>2d/inputmagic/mgc80.ofs</code></td><td>Magic glyph palette</td></tr>
      <tr><td>various</td><td><code>data/npc/NpcDataOfs.ofs</code></td><td>NPC personality / portrait data</td></tr>
      <tr><td>various</td><td><code>data/item/itemname.ofs</code></td><td>Item name strings</td></tr>
      <tr><td>map overlays</td><td><code>map/static.lzs</code></td><td>3D map textures</td></tr>
      <tr><td>map overlays</td><td><code>map/weather/*.ofs</code></td><td>Weather 3D models</td></tr>
      <tr><td>title screen</td><td><code>2d/mainmenu/title_pack.ofs</code></td><td>Title-screen background variants (5 seasons)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>title screen</td><td><code>title/titledata.lzs</code></td><td>Title splash sprites</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cache table entry layout (inferred)</h2>
  <p>Each slot in the master table is a struct accessed by:</p>
  <pre><code>{`struct CacheEntry {
    u32   flags;
    void *data_ptr;            // points into a heap-allocated decompressed RESO blob
    u32   size;
    u32   path_hash_or_id;
    ...
};`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Exact layout has not been fully decoded; the loader and consumers
    agree on offsets via <code>LDR/STR</code> with specific
    <code>[rN, #imm]</code> offsets (e.g. <code>[r5, #0x84]</code> for the
    item-icon sub-index).
  </p>

  <h2>Generic asset loader at <code>0x02052D20</code></h2>
  <p>Disassembly (THUMB, item-icon site):</p>
  <pre><code>{`02052D4C  LDR  R0, [PC, #0x30]      ; r0 = 0x020AA740   (master table)
02052D4E  LDR  R1, [PC, #0x34]      ; r1 = 0x020A55D8   ("item/itemicon.ofs")
02052D50  LSLS R3, R3, #0xA          ; r3 = 0x7800       (flags / type_code)
02052D52  BLX  0x02009894            ; call generic file-loader
                                     ; r2 = u16 sub-index from caller's [r5+0x84]
`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>notes/phaseA_ghidra/DISCOVERIES.md</code> — cache + loader analysis</li>
    <li><code>arm9_full_plaintext.bin</code> @ <code>0x02009894</code> — generic loader</li>
    <li><code>arm9_full_plaintext.bin</code> @ <code>0x02052D20</code> — item-icon loader thunk</li>
  </ul>
</FieldGuideLayout>
